('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000601', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What is the primary language for modern iOS development?', '["Objective-C", "Swift", "C#", "Kotlin"]', 'Swift', 'Swift is the powerful and intuitive programming language for iOS, macOS, and beyond.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000602', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'simple', 'mcq', 'In SwiftUI, which wrapper is used for simple local state?', '["@ObservedObject", "@State", "@Environment", "@Binding"]', '@State', '@State is a property wrapper for local state management within a single view.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000603', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What keyword defines a constant in Swift?', '["var", "const", "let", "fix"]', 'let', 'In Swift, "let" is used for constants and "var" for variables.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000604', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'simple', 'mcq', 'Which view is the root container for stacking items vertically in SwiftUI?', '["HStack", "ZStack", "VStack", "List"]', 'VStack', 'VStack (Vertical Stack) arranges children in a vertical line.', 'active'),
-- Intermediate
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000605', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is optional chaining in Swift?', '["Process of calling properties on an optional that might be nil", "Forcing an optional to have a value", "Checking if a variable is nil", "Defining a default value for an optional"]', 'Process of calling properties on an optional that might be nil', 'Optional chaining (?) allows you to query properties and methods on an optional without runtime crash if nil.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000606', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What does the @Binding property wrapper do in SwiftUI?', '["Stores a value persistently", "Creates a read/write connection to a state owned elsewhere", "Injects values from the environment", "Observes an external object"]', 'Creates a read/write connection to a state owned elsewhere', '@Binding creates a link between a source of truth and a view that displays and changes that data.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000607', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is the purpose of a Guard statement in Swift?', '["To define a loop", "To exit a function early if conditions aren''t met", "To handle asynchronous code", "To catch exceptions"]', 'To exit a function early if conditions aren''t met', 'Guard statements provide an early exit from a function, improving readability by reducing nested if-statements.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000608', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'intermediate', 'code_mcq', 'What will this code print?\nlet names = ["Apple", "Orange"]\nprint(names[safe: 2] ?? "None")', '["None", "Apple", "Index out of bounds", "nil"]', 'None', 'Assuming a common safe-index extension, it defaults to the nil-coalescing value "None" if index is out of bounds.', 'active'),
-- Expert
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000609', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is a "Retain Cycle" in Swift?', '["A loop that never ends", "A memory leak where two objects hold strong references to each other", "A cache policy", "Refreshing the UI loop"]', 'A memory leak where two objects hold strong references to each other', 'A retain cycle occurs when ARC cannot release objects because they point to each other with strong references.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000610', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the difference between "self" and "Self" in Swift?', '["self is the instance, Self is the type", "They are identical", "Self is the instance, self is the type", "Self is for SwiftUI only"]', 'self is the instance, Self is the type', 'Lowercase "self" refers to the specific instance, while uppercase "Self" refers to the type currently being used.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000611', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'expert', 'mcq', 'In SwiftUI, what is the purpose of the "@ViewBuilder" attribute?', '["To allow multiple views to be returned from a closure", "To optimize rendering", "To create custom view modifiers", "To handle user input events"]', 'To allow multiple views to be returned from a closure', '@ViewBuilder facilitates the construction of complex view hierarchies in a declarative manner.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000612', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'expert', 'code_mcq', 'Which property wrapper is used for data shared across the entire app environment?', '["@StateObject", "@ObservedObject", "@EnvironmentObject", "@State"]', '@EnvironmentObject', '@EnvironmentObject allows views to access shared data without explicit injection at every level.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000613', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000033', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the "Copy-on-Write" (CoW) mechanism in Swift?', '["Optimization where value types are only copied when modified", "Automatic duplication of data", "Mechanism for thread-safety", "Encryption of sensitive data"]', 'Optimization where value types are only copied when modified', 'CoW reduces memory usage by sharing the same internal storage for similar values until one of them is changed.', 'active');

