('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000622', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000034', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is Core Data Multithreading?', '["Running database on GPU", "Using multiple contexts on different queues to avoid UI blocking", "Recursive data entry", "Automatic cloud sync"]', 'Using multiple contexts on different queues to avoid UI blocking', 'Background contexts allow heavy data operations without freezing the main UI thread.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000623', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000034', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is "Batching" in Core Data?', '["Processing data in chunks", "Deleting multiple rows", "Updating many records at once without loading into memory", "Grouping views"]', 'Updating many records at once without loading into memory', 'Batch updates/deletes improve performance for large-scale data modifications.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000624', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000034', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the "Responder Chain" in iOS?', '["A sequence of network requests", "A hierarchy of objects that can handle events", "The database relationship chain", "User authentication flow"]', 'A hierarchy of objects that can handle events', 'The responder chain allows events to bubble up from a specific view to higher-level objects.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000625', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000034', 'expert', 'code_mcq', 'How do you create a custom UIView with UIKit?', '["class MyView: SwiftUI.View", "class MyView: UIView", "struct MyView: View", "UIView.make()"]', 'class MyView: UIView', 'Custom views in UIKit are created by subclassing UIView and overriding methods like draw(_:).', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000626', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000034', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is Core Data Migration?', '["Moving data to another database", "Adjusting the data model schema across versions", "Backing up data", "Data encryption process"]', 'Adjusting the data model schema across versions', 'Core Data migration handles transitions between different versions of an object model.', 'active');

