('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000636', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000035', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is "Recomposition" in Jetpack Compose?', '["Re-executing composable functions when data changes", "Restarting the app", "Compiling the code", "Updating the database"]', 'Re-executing composable functions when data changes', 'Recomposition is how Compose updates the UI when the underlying state changes.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000637', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000035', 'expert', 'mcq', 'In Kotlin, what does the "suspend" keyword do?', '["Marks a function that can be paused and resumed later", "Stops the thread", "Encrypts the function", "Makes it private"]', 'Marks a function that can be paused and resumed later', 'Suspend functions are the foundation of Kotlin Coroutines for non-blocking asynchronous work.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000638', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000035', 'expert', 'code_mcq', 'Which Flow operator is used to transform data in Kotlin?', '["filter", "map", "collect", "emit"]', 'map', 'The map operator transforms each emission into a new value.', 'active'),
