('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000648', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000036', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the "Task" and "Back Stack" in Android?', '["A way to manage multiple processes", "A collection of activities that users interact with when performing a certain job", "A database relationship", "A network queue"]', 'A collection of activities that users interact with when performing a certain job', 'Activities in a task are arranged in a stack (the back stack) in the order in which each activity is opened.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000649', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000036', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What are the main launch modes for an Activity?', '["standard, singleTop, singleTask, singleInstance", "basic, advanced, expert", "local, remote, proxy", "main, secondary, background"]', 'standard, singleTop, singleTask, singleInstance', 'Launch modes define how a new instance of an activity is associated with a current task.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000650', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000036', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the purpose of WorkManager?', '["To manage UI updates", "For deferrable, guaranteed background work", "To handle DNS resolution", "To build APKs"]', 'For deferrable, guaranteed background work', 'WorkManager is the recommended API for background processing that needs to be guaranteed to run.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000651', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000036', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is "Deep Linking" in Android?', '["Linking to a database", "Intents that send users directly to specific content within an app", "A type of encryption", "A network protocol"]', 'Intents that send users directly to specific content within an app', 'Deep links allow external sources to navigate users directly into your application.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000652', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000036', 'expert', 'code_mcq', 'Which method is called first when an Activity is starting?', '["onStart()", "onResume()", "onCreate()", "onRestart()"]', 'onCreate()', 'onCreate() is where you perform basic application startup logic that should happen only once.', 'active');

