-- Simple
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000653', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What is React Native?', '["A web framework", "A framework for building native mobile apps using JavaScript and React", "A database", "A compiler for Swift"]', 'A framework for building native mobile apps using JavaScript and React', 'React Native allows developers to use React to build high-quality native mobile experiences.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000654', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'simple', 'mcq', 'Which component is the basic building block for UI in React Native?', '["<div>", "View", "NativeBlock", "Canvas"]', 'View', 'The View component is the fundamental component for building UI, similar to a div in web.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000655', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'simple', 'mcq', 'How do you apply styles in React Native?', '["CSS files", "StyleSheet.create()", "Inline HTML styles", "SASS"]', 'StyleSheet.create()', 'React Native uses JavaScript objects for styling, usually abstracted into a StyleSheet.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000656', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What does the "Bridge" do in the old React Native architecture?', '["Connects JavaScript and Native threads via asynchronous JSON messages", "Compiles JS to Swift", "Manages the UI directly", "Speeds up the CPU"]', 'Connects JavaScript and Native threads via asynchronous JSON messages', 'The Bridge is the communication layer between the JS environment and the Native environment.', 'active'),
