('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000657', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is "TurboModules" in the new React Native architecture?', '["A faster type of Activity", "A more efficient way for JS to communicate with Native code using JSI", "A new UI layout engine", "A deployment tool"]', 'A more efficient way for JS to communicate with Native code using JSI', 'TurboModules improve startup time and performance by enabling synchronous communication.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000658', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is "Fabric" in the context of React Native?', '["A type of style", "The new rendering system for React Native", "A backend service", "A testing library"]', 'The new rendering system for React Native', 'Fabric is the new rendering engine that makes the UI more responsive and consistent.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000659', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is the purpose of Javascript Interface (JSI)?', '["To run JS in a browser", "To allow direct communication between JS and Native without the asynchronous bridge", "To animate the screen", "To manage networking"]', 'To allow direct communication between JS and Native without the asynchronous bridge', 'JSI is the core foundation for the new architecture, removing the overhead of JSON serialization.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000660', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'Which component would you use for a highly performant list in React Native?', '["ScrollView", "FlatList", "ListView (Deprecated)", "Column"]', 'FlatList', 'FlatList is optimized for large data sets by rendering only visible items.', 'active'),
-- Expert
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000661', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the "Yoga" layout engine?', '["A fitness app", "A cross-platform layout engine based on Flexbox used by React Native", "A database query language", "An animation library"]', 'A cross-platform layout engine based on Flexbox used by React Native', 'Yoga is used by React Native to calculate the position and size of UI components across platforms.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000662', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'expert', 'mcq', 'In the new architecture, what is "CodeGen"?', '["A tool to generate native code from JS types to ensure type safety between JS and C++", "An AI code generator", "A build tool for APKs", "A deployment script"]', 'A tool to generate native code from JS types to ensure type safety between JS and C++', 'CodeGen ensures both sides (JS and Native) are in sync with the same interfaces.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000663', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is "Hermes" in React Native?', '["A package manager", "An open-source JavaScript engine optimized for mobile apps", "A styling library", "A networking protocol"]', 'An open-source JavaScript engine optimized for mobile apps', 'Hermes significantly improves start-up time and reduces app size and memory usage.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000664', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'expert', 'mcq', 'How does "Native Modules" implementation differ between Android and iOS?', '["Android use Java/Kotlin, iOS uses Objective-C/Swift", "No difference", "They both use JS", "They both use Python"]', 'Android use Java/Kotlin, iOS uses Objective-C/Swift', 'Native modules require platform-specific implementations using the respective native languages.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000665', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000037', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the impact of "Shadow Trees" in React Native?', '["They manage lighting in the UI", "They represent the layout state of the UI before it is applied to native views", "They store logs", "They are for security"]', 'They represent the layout state of the UI before it is applied to native views', 'Shadow trees are used by the layout engine to calculate constraints before the actual native view injection.', 'active');

