('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000667', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'simple', 'mcq', 'Which widget is used to build a UI that doesn''t change its properties?', '["StatefulWidget", "StatelessWidget", "Container", "Box"]', 'StatelessWidget', 'StatelessWidgets are immutable, meaning their properties cannot change once built.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000668', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What language is used for writing Flutter apps?', '["Go", "Dart", "Swift", "Java"]', 'Dart', 'Dart is the language optimized for UI development used by Flutter.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000669', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What is the "pubspec.yaml" file for?', '["Configuring UI", "Managing dependencies and app metadata", "Writing logic", "Styling"]', 'Managing dependencies and app metadata', 'All libraries, images, and fonts used by a Flutter app are defined in pubspec.yaml.', 'active'),
-- Intermediate
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000670', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What does the "setState" method do in Flutter?', '["Saves data permanently", "Notifies the framework that the internal state of a widget has changed, triggering a rebuild", "Restarts the app", "Transitions to a new screen"]', 'Notifies the framework that the internal state of a widget has changed, triggering a rebuild', 'Calling setState is the most basic way to update the UI with new data in a StatefulWidget.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000671', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is "Provider" in Flutter?', '["A type of screen", "A popular state management library based on InheritedWidget", "A database", "A deployment script"]', 'A popular state management library based on InheritedWidget', 'Provider offers a cleaner way to share state than passing it manually through constructors.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000672', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is "Hot Reload"?', '["Reinstalling the app", "Applying code changes without restarting the app or losing its state", "Updating the OS", "Clearing cache"]', 'Applying code changes without restarting the app or losing its state', 'Hot Reload makes Flutter development extremely fast by sub-second UI updates.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000673', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is the purpose of "InheritedWidget"?', '["To build complex UI", "To provide data to its descendants efficiently without passing parameters", "To manage history", "To render images"]', 'To provide data to its descendants efficiently without passing parameters', 'InheritedWidget is the foundation of many state management libraries like Provider.', 'active'),
-- Expert
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000674', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is "Riverpod" and how is it different from Provider?', '["A networking library", "A rewrite of Provider that is compile-safe and doesn''t depend on the Flutter Context", "A styling library", "A cloud service"]', 'A rewrite of Provider that is compile-safe and doesn''t depend on the Flutter Context', 'Riverpod solves many limitations of Provider, like the need for a Widget tree to access state.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000675', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is BLoC (Business Logic Component) pattern?', '["A type of widget", "A state management pattern based on Streams/Sinks to separate UI from logic", "A build tool", "A testing framework"]', 'A state management pattern based on Streams/Sinks to separate UI from logic', 'BLoC promotes high testability and clean separation of concerns by using reactive programming.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000676', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What are Dart Isolates?', '["Threads that share memory", "Independent workers that do not share memory and communicate via ports", "A type of UI component", "A debugging tool"]', 'Independent workers that do not share memory and communicate via ports', 'Isolates are Dart''s way of performing multi-threaded work without the complexity of shared memory.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000677', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the purpose of the "CustomPainter" class?', '["To edit images", "To provide a canvas for drawing custom shapes and graphics", "To manage network states", "To handle user input"]', 'To provide a canvas for drawing custom shapes and graphics', 'CustomPainter allows for low-level drawing access within the Flutter widget tree.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000678', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000038', 'expert', 'mcq', 'In Dart, what is a "Mixin"?', '["A type of class that can be instantiated", "A way of reusing a class''s code in multiple class hierarchies", "A private variable", "A build script"]', 'A way of reusing a class''s code in multiple class hierarchies', 'Mixins are perfect for adding specific functionalities to multiple classes without complex inheritance.', 'active');

-- Topic 39: Mobile-First Design Patterns (13 Questions)
-- Simple
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000679', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What does "Mobile-First" design involve?', '["Designing for mobile screens first and scaling up to desktop", "Designing only for mobile", "Hiding desktop features", "Using small fonts"]', 'Designing for mobile screens first and scaling up to desktop', 'Mobile-first design prioritizes the mobile experience as the primary interface.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000680', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What is a "Hamburger Menu"?', '["A food ordering icon", "A navigation menu toggle frequently represented by three parallel horizontal lines", "A type of UI button", "A search filter"]', 'A navigation menu toggle frequently represented by three parallel horizontal lines', 'Hamburger menus save space by hiding navigation links behind a single icon.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000681', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What is the purpose of "Skeleton Screens"?', '["To show a loading spinner", "To provide a visual placeholder while content is loading", "To show the app structure for developers", "A diagnostic tool"]', 'To provide a visual placeholder while content is loading', 'Skeleton screens reduce perceived wait time by showing the layout structure early.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000682', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What is "Dark Mode" in mobile UI?', '["A way to turn off the phone", "A light-on-dark color scheme for the interface", "A battery saving app", "A privacy filter"]', 'A light-on-dark color scheme for the interface', 'Dark mode reduces eye strain and improves battery life on OLED screens.', 'active'),
-- Intermediate
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000683', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'Which design pattern is commonly used for complex navigation in mobile apps?', '["Tab Bar / Bottom Navigation", "Horizontal scrolling lists only", "Popups for everything", "Single page scroll"]', 'Tab Bar / Bottom Navigation', 'Bottom navigation provides consistent access to main app sections on mobile devices.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000684', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is the "Thumb Zone" in mobile design?', '["The area where the phone is manufactured", "The area of the screen most easily reached by a thumb during one-handed use", "A finger print scanner", "The charging port"]', 'The area of the screen most easily reached by a thumb during one-handed use', 'Designing around the thumb zone ensures the app remains ergonomic and easy to use.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000685', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is "Haptic Feedback"?', '["A type of visual animation", "Physical vibrations/pulses to give the user tactile confirmation of actions", "An audio sound effect", "A push notification"]', 'Physical vibrations/pulses to give the user tactile confirmation of actions', 'Haptics enhance the user experience by grounding digital actions in physical sensations.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000686', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is a "Modal" in mobile apps?', '["A background thread", "A temporary UI element that sits on top of the main content and prevents interaction with it", "A menu item", "A type of database model"]', 'A temporary UI element that sits on top of the main content and prevents interaction with it', 'Modals are used for focused user tasks or notifications that require immediate attention.', 'active'),
-- Expert
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000687', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the "Adaptive Layout" pattern?', '["Changing the UI colors based on time of day", "Designing the UI to adjust specifically to different screen sizes and orientations", "Using AI to design the UI", "A layout that moves randomly"]', 'Designing the UI to adjust specifically to different screen sizes and orientations', 'Adaptive layouts ensure the app looks and functions well on phones, foldables, and tablets.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000688', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is "Micro-interaction" in UX?', '["A large complex animation", "Small, subtle responses to user actions that provide feedback and polish", "A database query", "A network handshake"]', 'Small, subtle responses to user actions that provide feedback and polish', 'Micro-interactions make the interface feel alive and state-aware.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000689', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the intent of "Progressive Disclosure"?', '["Showing all data at once", "Initially showing only essential info and revealing more as requested", "Hiding data forever", "A security leak"]', 'Initially showing only essential info and revealing more as requested', 'Progressive disclosure prevents information overload and reduces cognitive load.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000690', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'expert', 'mcq', 'Explain "Anticipatory Design" in the context of mobile apps.', '["Design that is slow to respond", "Design that predicts user needs and offers actions or content before they search for it", "A classic retro style", "A design for robots"]', 'Design that predicts user needs and offers actions or content before they search for it', 'Anticipatory design uses data and context to simplify the user journey.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000691', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000039', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is the "Golden Ratio" used for in UI design?', '["Calculating screen brightness", "A mathematical ratio used to create balanced, aesthetically pleasing layouts and grids", "To set the app price", "A security standard"]', 'A mathematical ratio used to create balanced, aesthetically pleasing layouts and grids', 'The golden ratio (approx 1.618) helps create organic-looking proportions in UI components.', 'active');

-- Topic 40: App Performance & Publishing (9 Questions)
-- Simple
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000692', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What is an "APK" in Android?', '["A design document", "Android Package Kit, the file format used to distribute and install apps", "A compiler error", "A type of icon"]', 'Android Package Kit, the file format used to distribute and install apps', 'APKs are the standard binaries for Android app installation.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000693', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What is Apple''s official store for publishing iOS apps?', '["Play Store", "Cydia", "App Store", "iTunes (only)"]', 'App Store', 'The App Store is the strictly governed marketplace for iOS applications.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000694', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'simple', 'mcq', 'What is "App Indexing"?', '["A type of UI list", "Allowing search engines to index app content and deep link to it", "Counting the number of users", "Sorting code files"]', 'Allowing search engines to index app content and deep link to it', 'App indexing improves app visibility in general web search results.', 'active'),
-- Intermediate
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000695', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is "A/B Testing" for mobile apps?', '["A design choice", "A method of comparing two versions of an app to see which performs better", "Testing on Android and then B (iOS)", "Checking for bugs A and B"]', 'A method of comparing two versions of an app to see which performs better', 'A/B testing helps in making data-driven decisions regarding UI and feature efficacy.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000696', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is an "Android App Bundle" (.aab)?', '["A zip file of images", "A publishing format that optimizes the APK for each device configuration", "A developer license", "A type of UI widget"]', 'A publishing format that optimizes the APK for each device configuration', 'App Bundles result in smaller install sizes for users by serving only needed resources.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000697', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'intermediate', 'mcq', 'What is "TestFlight" used for?', '["Designing UI on a flight", "Apple''s beta testing service to distribute apps to testers", "A testing framework for Java", "A performance monitoring tool"]', 'Apple''s beta testing service to distribute apps to testers', 'TestFlight allows developers to gather feedback before the public release on the App Store.', 'active'),
-- Expert
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000698', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'expert', 'mcq', 'How do you analyze "Memory Leaks" in Android?', '["By looking at logs only", "Using tools like LeakCanary or the Android Profiler", "By restarting the phone", "By asking users"]', 'Using tools like LeakCanary or the Android Profiler', 'Memory profiling tools help identify objects that are not being garbage collected.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000699', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'expert', 'mcq', 'Explain "App Thinning" on iOS.', '["Making the phone thinner", "A process that combines slicing, bitcode, and on-demand resources to minimize app size", "Removing features", "Using low-res images"]', 'A process that combines slicing, bitcode, and on-demand resources to minimize app size', 'App thinning ensures that users only download the content necessary for their specific device hardware.', 'active'),
('60000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000700', '50000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000040', 'expert', 'mcq', 'What is "Bitcode" for iOS publishing?', '["A type of bit currency", "An intermediate representation of a compiled program that allows Apple to re-optimize app binaries for hardware", "A security code", "A compression algorithm"]', 'An intermediate representation of a compiled program that allows Apple to re-optimize app binaries for hardware', 'Bitcode allows Apple to re-compile and optimize apps for new device architectures without requiring a new upload from the developer.', 'active');


